<title>NORWAY: Statoil expands VLCC fleet to four.</title>
<headline>Statoil expands VLCC fleet to four.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil ) said on Thursday it had added the supertankers Siam and Berge Stadt to its fleet, primarily to transport crude across the Atlantic to Canada and the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>Built in 1993, the 300,000-tonne Siam has a doule hull and is owned by World Wide Shipping in Singapore. It is chartered for two years with options for another year.</p>
<p>Double-hulled Berge Stadt is owned by Norway's Bergesen d.y. Group and was built in 1994. The 307,000- deadweight tonne vessel will begin its charter to Statoil in the autumn, the company's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>Statoil said the new additions brought the group's fleet of very large crude carriers to four.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
